cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this framework, its dataset or its results, please cite it."
title: "Bone scaffolds — property prediction and inverse design"
abstract: >-
  Predicts the mechanical and degradation behaviour of biopolymer bone
  scaffolds from composition, process and architecture, then runs that model
  backwards to propose a scaffold worth printing. Combines a voxel FEM sweep
  over TPMS and FDM architectures, a mechanistic decoder with zero learned
  parameters, multi-fidelity co-kriging, and validation that is grouped by
  publication and by architecture rather than random.
type: software
